Description: guard __NR_mseal with defined() check in sandbox syscall_sets
 mseal (kernel 6.10+) is absent from older kernel uapi headers (UOS
 loong64 headers); a bare `case __NR_mseal:` fails to compile there.
 Guard it like the sw64 support patch does. Harmless on newer headers.
Author: pengfeixx
Forwarded: no
--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/sandbox/linux/seccomp-bpf-helpers/syscall_sets.cc
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/sandbox/linux/seccomp-bpf-helpers/syscall_sets.cc
@@ -558,7 +558,9 @@
     case __NR_mlock:
     case __NR_munlock:
     case __NR_munmap:
+#if defined(__NR_mseal)
     case __NR_mseal:
+#endif
       return true;
     case __NR_madvise:
     case __NR_mincore:
